{"agent":"fix-autoresume","data":{"item":"fix-Bbc611c0165","redactions":1,"relayed_by":"","text":"Fix ddflow bug Bbc611c0165 (HIGH): background orchestrator lanes lose their self-scheduled resume when their turn completes, so their claim lapses and re-interrupts. Pass as_agent=fix-autoresume on EVERY ddflow call; HOLD claims with ddflow heartbeat <id>. Research FIRST: read ddflow/services/lanes + ddflow/services/driver + ddflow/services/waves (the lane-driver resume/wave loop) and understand how a lane schedules its next resume (schedule_wakeup / ddflow resume) and what happens when the subagent turn ends. Confirm the failure mode: the resume is dropped at turn completion. Then choose the fix (prefer: keep the lane session alive and loop internally until its scope drains, so it never completes prematurely; if the harness drops wakeups at completion, the lane must not rely on them). Write the regression test FIRST (fails on unfixed): a lane that schedules a resume actually resumes, and its claim stays heartbeat-held/live rather than lapsing to INTERRUPTED. Verify it fails before the fix and passes after. Then grok/x.ai + gemini/google cross-family review (export GEMINI_API_KEY from [REDACTED:path] first), scoped ddflow unit_tests <selected> BEFORE merge, merge, complete --model deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila --regression-test <test>. Report merge sha.\n"},"id":"e593c9390ac670a261ceb35f3","kind":"session.prompt","lamport":149479,"schema":1,"subject":"s20261107T151015-221622","ts":"2026-11-07T15:10:16.404126Z"}
